Given the pattern used elsewhere (e.g., the rendering loop passes a `dt` to its update functions), it makes sense to give `updateDOM` an explicit `dt` parameter, defaulting to a typical 60 fps step (`1/60`). That way, existing calls that don’t pass a value will continue to work, while new calls can supply the precise delta time.

